      "side": 1,
      "message": "Cloud name is used directly to build `filename \u003d f\"{cloud}_{name}.json\"` and then joined into both `Config[\"json_web_path\"]` and `REMOTE_DIR`. `POST /api/v3/clouds/` (clouds.py:60-80) accepts any non-empty string with no charset validation, so a cloud named `foo/../../etc/...` makes this plugin read/write outside the intended directories (and we write as root on the tenant host). Suggest `re.fullmatch(r\"[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\", cloud)` (or at least `os.path.basename()`) before path use.",
      "revId": "507fa047873007a586df936f8b7901bd3aa38c8d",
